    "conclusion":  "The M178 straight east-side route collides with the M-04 pantry block in the existing bath-first room-block alternative. A dogleg shifts west before the pantry begins and continues along the dining east edge; it clears the modeled pantry, furniture and wall rectangles while retaining the nominal porch door. The dogleg has a 21 in transverse spill beyond the dining width below the pantry and relies on the proposed absence of east-side dining chairs. No room layout or route is selected.",
    "limitations":  [
                        "Bath-first blocks are unapproved and larger than owner room-area targets; coordinate overlay is comparative only.",
                        "Dining leg is tangent to the 36 in table edge envelope and depends on no east-side chair; pulled-back seating and people are not measured.",
                        "The 21 in transition spill is unassigned and may conflict with other rooms or shell boundaries.",
                        "Porch door is a nominal 5 ft reservation, not a verified clear opening. Appliance-open envelopes, wall construction, threshold, shell, site, service routes, Revit and IFC are not validated.",
                        "M-06/B remains unassigned; no code compliance, accessibility, structural safety, certification, permit approval or construction readiness is established."
